Under the policy, the coverage duration for pre-hospitalization expenses is up to 30 days immediately before your admission to the hospital for the same illness, provided that an inpatient hospitalization claim has been accepted. For post-hospitalization expenses, the coverage duration can vary, allowing for expenses to be covered for up to 60 days, 90 days, or 180 days after discharge from the hospital, depending on the specific terms of your plan. Inpatient hospitalization treatment covers a range of medical expenses, including room and boarding in a private air-conditioned room, ICU expenses, nursing fees, fees for surgeons and anesthetists, costs for anesthesia, blood, oxygen, operation theatre charges, dialysis, chemotherapy, physiotherapy, prescription drugs, artificial limbs, and necessary diagnostic tests like X-rays.
